&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tech Risk Officer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Adyen combines the agility of a global tech company with the stability of a licensed financial institution. As a Tech Risk Officer focused on AI technology, you will partner with cross-functional teams and regional second-line functions (such as Model risk, Compliance and the DPO office) to ensure safe, secure, and resilient implementation of autonomous AI architectures and regulatory requirements.&lt;br&gt;The Tech Risk team, part of the second line risk function ensures that risk management practices are applied across Adyen’s technological environments, teams and initiatives. This continuous task requires a close and supporting relationship with tech teams in the first line, in order to understand changes in the tech landscape but also to guide them in relation to risk mitigations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;In this role, you will focus on the unique security and architectural risks associated with building, deploying, and monitoring autonomous AI agents, working closely with first-line engineering teams to embed risk mitigation into technical design. You will be part of building technology, challenging design and execution through constructive and positive conversations. Realize better outcomes together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate is a risk or tech professional with hands-on experience evaluating and managing risks arising from the implementation of AI solutions, software architecture for agentic systems and the underlying tech stack. You have a technical background that enables you to evaluate agentic workflows, models safety, and integration points, advancing our second-line risk framework to support safe AI innovation at scale. Both security as well as IT-resilience experience is welcome.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate technology threats and risks &amp;nbsp;across diverse AI developments in the industry, internal projects and assets, advising stakeholders and ensuring risk mitigation actions are implemented.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with leadership and build an internal network to ensure the domain remains represented in business activities, contributing to decision making.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the second line risk oversight for AI and general Technology risks, including KRI design, risk monitoring and reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other Risk domains, in order to incorporate AI Tech risks into Adyen’s risk profile, ensuring those are considered when evaluating company objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with or advise other second-line teams (typically Regulatory, Compliance and Privacy) in the implementation of AI Governance requirements in Adyen’s tech environments, as well as engage with local auditors or external partners (externally) as a trusted point of contact for the specific risk domain, globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with various regulators to provide clarity on Adyen’s IT Resilience and excellence landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 5+ years experience within a risk management function, with 2 years of demonstrated experience guiding AI risk mitigations, AI Governance or AI Cyber Security. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience evaluating technology risks, Security best practices and associated industry and regulatory frameworks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You feel comfortable explaining risks associated with IT environments to engineers but also to business stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a solid understanding of commonly used AI technology stack (hardware, software, network and systems, on-prem or cloud solutions), at the level required to identify risks or weaknesses and recommend tangible actions, design metrics to enable risk monitoring and oversight.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are innovative, flexible with strong problem-solving capabilities and able to define effective processes, when possible scaling manual processes via automation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work from our &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New York&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;office and travel to other offices periodically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English, both written and spoken. Any additional language is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
