&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer - Java Application Core Components (JACC)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adyen provides a global, unified platform built by Java application teams across the company. The Java Application Core Components (JACC) team plays a key role in this: we build and maintain the shared frameworks and components that define how other Adyen teams design, structure, and deploy their Java applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of JACC, you will build and maintain the core Java tools and components used across all of Adyen, shaping how other engineering teams build their services. You&#39;ll work on some of the largest ongoing efforts in the company, including 3 large-scale migrations that will shape the future of Adyen&#39;s application architecture. You&#39;ll join a lean team of 6 Java experts, working in a Kanban-like way with minimal process overhead, and gain real influence over the architecture of one of the leading players in the payments space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and evolve the internal and open source Java frameworks and components used by every Java application team at Adyen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play an active role in one or more of the team&#39;s 3 large-scale migrations that are reshaping Adyen&#39;s application architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical guidance to other engineering teams, by guiding them on how the frameworks and libraries we provide can be used to solve Adyen&#39;s business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve workflows used by other engineering teams across Adyen, working closely with them to identify pain points and improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with partner platform teams (Kubernetes infrastructure, deployment, security) to make sure our components integrate well across Adyen&#39;s tech stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for best practices across Adyen and define boundaries/guidance on how the frameworks/libraries we maintain can be used. This should be achieved by creating code validation rules, running workshops and giving presentations to other development teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
