&lt;p&gt;Adyen provides payments, data, and financial products in a single solution for customers like Meta, Uber, H&amp;amp;M, and Microsoft - making us the financial technology platform of choice. At Adyen, everything we do is engineered for ambition.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For our teams, we create an environment with opportunities for our people to succeed, backed by the culture and support to ensure they are enabled to truly own their careers. We are motivated individuals who tackle unique technical challenges at scale and solve them as a team. Together, we deliver innovative and ethical solutions that help businesses achieve their ambitions faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Compliance Manager, Scheme Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a senior, strategic, and product-minded leader to head the global Growth pillar within Schemes Compliance. This role sits at the intersection of compliance, product, partnerships, and commercial strategy enabling business growth while ensuring scalable, well-controlled solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a globally distributed team who unlock new products, markets, local payment methods, and partner models by designing compliant operating models, accelerating launches, and building scalable solutions in close collaboration with Product and Engineering. You will work closely with Commercial and Sales to identify merchant needs and revenue opportunities, ensuring merchant demand directly shapes our growth priorities and builds a roadmap. Many of our growth initiatives are driven by strategic merchants whose needs influence where we invest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Product Compliance Manager, Scheme Compliance, you will act as a key bridge between compliance and product, translating regulatory, scheme, and partner requirements into systems, frameworks, and tooling that enable speed without compromising control, and help shape how Adyen approaches new and emerging payment models globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and scale a globally distributed team focused on enabling growth initiatives across products, geographies, and payment methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the growth strategy for Scheme Compliance, working with cross-functional leaders to prioritize new product launches, market expansion, and onboarding of payment methods and financial partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Commercial and Sales to identify high-value merchant needs and revenue opportunities, translating merchant demand into clear growth priorities, requirements, and build decisions for Product and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product and Engineering to define payment flows, data models, and configuration standards that embed compliance requirements into systems rather than manual processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and standardize operating models for new business lines, including clear control points, monitoring requirements, and defensible documentation for regulators and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional programs across Commercial, Partnerships, Legal, Risk, and Product to accelerate time-to-market for strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an escalation point for complex or ambiguous growth opportunities, balancing speed, risk, and commercial impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify friction in existing payments compliance or partner requirements and proactively design solutions or influence changes to unlock growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear frameworks for decision-making (e.g., what to launch, constrain, or decline), ensuring consistency across regions and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build playbooks, tooling requirements, and training programs to increase organizational fluency in growth-related compliance topics.&lt;/li&gt;
