&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Partner Solutions Engineer, Hardware&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adyen is looking for a Senior Partner Solutions Engineer with a track record of hands-on embedded Android or systems engineering work to own the technical relationship with one or more of our most complex hardware OEM partners. You&#39;ll be the primary technical authority on that relationship: root-causing the hardest device-level issues, holding senior OEM engineering counterparts accountable, and shaping how Adyen manages OEM technical relationships as the function grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Adyen evolves its hardware offerings and moves toward a hardware independence model, this role carries real weight. Your OEM relationship is one of the more demanding ones in the portfolio, and you&#39;re expected to bring judgment and strategy to it, not just execute an existing playbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary, most senior technical advisor for your OEM&#39;s engineering team, leading escalations on the most complex device-level issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical strategy for your OEM relationship: which issues to prioritize, which process gaps to close, and how automation and tooling should evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional alignment across Product, Engineering, Hardware Integrity/Reliability, and Commercial on priorities for your OEM, especially when those priorities conflict.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and drive adoption of tooling, automation, and process improvements that scale quality efforts across the relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Commercial to drive proactive improvements to the Adyen payment experience on partner devices, not just reactive bug-fixing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other Partner Solutions Engineers on debugging approach and partner management, without formal management responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the broader and scalable operating model for Hardware Partner Engineering as Adyen adds OEM relationships and device coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in a technical solutions role, partner engineering, or related fields, with proven experience in a customer-facing role (e.g., developer advocate, partner engineer, technical solutions engineer, or solutions architect).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of hands-on embedded, firmware, or systems engineering experience, with meaningful exposure to hardware, embedded, or device-level environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded Android experience in a point-of-sale context (e.g. point-of-sale terminals, payment terminals, kiosks, unattended/vending machines, etc.) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A credible technical authority who can evaluate an OEM&#39;s root-cause claims and hold senior OEM engineering counterparts accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of turning a reactive backlog into durable process, tooling, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator, comfortable leading discussions with senior partner engineering leadership and internal cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and a strategic mindset: you&#39;re thinking a few steps past the current ticket queue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel to OEM locations and work across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
