&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Partnerships Manager - Visa&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adyen is looking for a Senior Partnerships Manager who will advance Adyen’s strategy and agenda with Visa globally. In this role, you will lead high-impact Visa partnerships for Adyen and use your expertise and influence to build strong inroads across their global organization. You will serve as a recognized subject matter expert whose insights help shape our partnership strategy, while working together with a broad range of senior cross-functional stakeholders across Product, Commercial, and Finance teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time position based in our London or Amsterdam office reporting into our Head of Card Network &amp;amp; Product Partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Partnership Management: Build and nurture deep global relationships with Visa across all levels. Architect and execute multi-year strategic plans for key initiatives and establish partnership frameworks to ensure Adyen remains at the forefront of payments innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver High-Impact Outcomes: Drive breakthrough commercial performance and long-term financial scalability for our Visa portfolio. Solve complex, ambiguous payment ecosystem challenges by leveraging deep analytical insight into scheme economics, scheme fees, and incentive structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Strategy &amp;amp; Innovation: Serve as a key strategic advisor to Product. Deeply shape our product roadmap through expert network insights and the co-creation of novel joint solutions across card acquiring, issuing, and digital payment technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership &amp;amp; GTM: Lead complex cross-functional initiatives across commercial, product, finance, and legal teams to execute high-stakes go-to-market strategies and support major merchant opportunities globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thought Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship: Act as a thought leader and mentor for Partnership Managers across the organization. Lead strategic internal projects that elevate Adyen’s partnership capabilities and industry reputation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience in strategic partnerships or business development in the payments industry, with a track record of handling complex global relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess strong domain expertise across card acquiring and issuing, together with a strong understanding of payment ecosystem dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in negotiating complex, multi-year bespoke agreements together with global card network and/or fintech partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate ecosystem trends into clear commercial models and actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and negotiation skills, together with the ability to influence both internal and external leadership across different functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with extensive autonomy in a fast-paced environment, with a track record of inspiring virtual cross-functional teams without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An MBA or equivalent advanced degree is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full professional proficiency (written and verbal) in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
