&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Lead - Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;As a Software Engineering Team Lead based in Singapore, you will lead a team of highly skilled software engineers responsible for building and evolving Adyen’s Alternative Payment Methods (APMs) platform for the APAC region. Your team plays a critical role in enabling merchants to offer a broad range of local and global payment methods, helping businesses reach more customers and deliver seamless payment experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with Product Managers, Architects and Engineering teams to develop and scale integrations with alternative payment methods, including digital wallets, bank transfers, real-time payment schemes and other locally relevant payment solutions. You&#39;ll drive the technical direction of the team, ensuring our payment capabilities remain scalable, reliable and maintainable as we expand into new markets and support evolving payment methods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a people leader, you&#39;ll coach and develop engineers, foster a culture of ownership, and guide the team through complex technical challenges. As part of Adyen&#39;s global engineering organisation, you&#39;ll collaborate with teams across Europe, APAC and North America to build payment solutions that scale globally while meeting the specific needs of local markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and develop a team of Software Engineers, supporting their technical and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a high-performing engineering culture built on ownership, collaboration and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Managers to translate business priorities and market needs into scalable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the technical direction of the team, balancing product delivery with long-term platform scalability, resilience and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide architectural discussions and engineering decisions relating to APM integrations, payment processing and platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve integrations with alternative payment methods, including local payment schemes, digital wallets, bank transfers and other regional payment solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure payment integrations are reliable, secure and scalable, with appropriate handling of payment flows, transaction statuses, errors and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering Managers, Architects and Team Leads across Adyen to improve engineering practices and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an escalation point for complex technical challenges, helping the team navigate ambiguity and make thoughtful engineering trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve engineering quality through better testing, observability, operational excellence and developer productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Adyen&#39;s APM strategy in APAC, balancing local market requirements and payment method expansion with long-term platform scalability, resilience and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Who you are&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience leading and developing high-performing software engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong software engineering background building large-scale, distributed systems using Java or similar backend technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy coaching engineers through technical mentorship, regular feedback and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable leading technical discussions, facilitating architectural decisions and balancing engineering quality with business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working closely with Product Managers and cross-functional stakeholders to deliver customer-focused solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong problem-solving skills and enjoy tackling complex technical challenges at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
