&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data is Adyen&#39;s key differentiator, but to unlock its full potential, we are executing a fundamental technical and cultural shift. We are accelerating toward a strong &lt;strong&gt;Data Foundation&lt;/strong&gt; model where every domain owns the data it produces, treats it as a product, and guarantees its quality at the source through enforceable data contracts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Technical Program Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be the operational engine driving our Data Foundations set-up. You will own the cross-functional execution framework required to establish robust data governance, support the rollout of self-service data infrastructure, drive organizational adoption, and systematically reduce technical debt across Adyen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Execution at Pace&lt;/strong&gt;: Take full ownership of the Data Foundation program, effectively unblocking teams so they can focus on building rather than navigating dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge Gaps &amp;amp; Silos&lt;/strong&gt;: Oversee and drive alignment across multiple solutions where you identify and manage dependencies that individual product teams might overlook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mitigate Risk&lt;/strong&gt;: Ensure risks of the program are mitigated promptly and proactively to avoid impact of delays or incorrect technical decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultural transformation and adoption&lt;/strong&gt;: drive change management across the organization in the way we see, store and use data to ensure it fits our Data Strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Debt &amp;amp; Modernization&lt;/strong&gt;: coordinate milestones for legacy systems deprecation, to ensure we reduce technical debt while focusing on driving the modernization of our Data Tech Stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Artifacts&lt;/strong&gt;: Establish and maintain standardized program health tools, including RAID logs (Risks, Actions, Issues, Dependencies), program dashboards, new blue-prints and cross-team roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Technical Program Management Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; 5–7 years of experience leading complex, high-stakes technical programs or platform migrations in global, cross-product environments (preferably Tech).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Functional understanding of modern data design patterns and infrastructure, including Data Mesh, Data Contracts, lineage tracking, and metadata cataloging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Management &amp;amp; Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong ability to navigate across the organization, foster collaboration and alignment, and align product and engineering teams to adopt a &quot;data as a product&quot; mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent capability to look across individual products, synthesize dependencies, trade-offs and ensure all is managed from one centralized roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metrics-Driven Operator:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong analytical skills with a proven track record of establishing standardized telemetry, RAID logs, and program dashboards to monitor execution velocity and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
